From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:38:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] moe: --moe-cache-batch and a per-request moe_cache_batch
 for the server

The largest ubatch the MoE cache serves was a constant (32 tokens): bigger
prompts stage every expert of every layer through the GPU, a scan of the
whole expert pool. The limit is now a context parameter with a setter, a
server flag, and a request field, so a client that knows a short prompt
starts long work (an agent turn, a coding task) can raise it and keep the
cache warm, while a document dump still takes the staged path.
